hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24056","Narrated to us Hushaym, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, narrated to me Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud: Shroud them in their clothes. He said: And he would bury a group in the grave. He said: And he said: Put forward the most Quran of them."
"24057","Narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, informed to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the slain of Uhud, he said: I bear witness over these. There is no wounded who is wounded in Allah, Mighty and Majestic, except Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection, his wound bleeding, the color the color of blood, and the smell the smell of musk. Look for the most جمعا of them of the Quran, and put him before them in the grave."
"24058","Narrated to us Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Abi Suayr, and Mamar confirmed it to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the slain of Uhud and said: I bear witness over these. Shroud them with their wounds and their blood."
"24059","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Suayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: When it was the day of Uhud, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the martyrs who were killed that day and said: Shroud them with their blood, for I have borne witness over them. So two men and three would be buried in one grave, and it would be asked: Which of them was most reciting of the Quran? So they would put him forward. Jabir said: So my father and my uncle were buried that day in one grave."
"24060","Narrated to us Yazid, informed to us Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to me al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr, that Abu Jahl said when the people met: O Allah, the severest of us in kinship, and who brought us what we do not know, destroy him in the morning. So he was the one seeking judgment."
"24061","Narrated to us Yaqub, narrated to us my father, from Ibn Ishaq, narrated to me Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr al-Udhri, and in what he read to Yaqub, al-Udhri, ally of Banu Zuhrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the people of Uhud, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Yazid."
"24062","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Said, from Uthman, narrated to us a man in the circle of Abu Uthman, he said: Saad, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that they were commanded to fast a day. Then a man came in part of the day and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so and so-and-so have been exhausted. So he turned away from him, and he mentioned the hadith."
"24063","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Ibn Jurayj, he said: And Ibn Shihab said: Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr al-Udhri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people two days before al-Fitr and said: Give a sa of wheat or grain between two, or a sa of dates, or a sa of barley, upon every free and slave, small and large."
"24064","Narrated to us Affan, he said: I asked Hammad ibn Zayd about the charity of al-Fitr, so he narrated to me from Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Thalabah ibn Abi Suayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give a sa of wheat or a sa of burr. And Hammad doubted: from every two, small or large, male or female, free or owned, rich or poor. As for your rich, Allah will purify him, and as for your poor, more than what he gives will be returned to him."
"24065","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: Yunus read it to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdullah ibn Thalabah informed me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped his face, that he saw Saad ibn Abi Waqqas praying witr with one rakah, not adding to it, until he would stand in the middle of the night."
"24066","Narrated to us Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Harb, narrated to me al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr al-Udhri, he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped his face at the time of the Conquest."
"24067","Narrated to us Abu al-Yaman, narrated to us Shuayb, from al-Zuhri, narrated to me Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr al-Udhri, he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped his face at the time of the Conquest, that he saw Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, Saad had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), praying witr with one rakah after the Isha prayer, meaning al-Atamah, not adding to it, until he would stand in the middle of the night."
"24068","Narrated to us Abu al-Yaman, narrated to us Shuayb, from al-Zuhri, narrated to me Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr al-Udhri, he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped his face at the time of the Conquest, that he saw Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, Saad had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), praying witr with one rakah after the Isha prayer, meaning al-Atamah, not adding to it, until he would stand in the middle of the night."
"24069","Narrated to us Hajjaj, narrated to us Layth, meaning Ibn Saad, narrated to me Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr al-Udhri, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped over his face, and he met the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: They used to forbid me from the kiss, fearing that I would draw near to more than it. Then the Muslims today forbid it, and a speaker says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had from the protection of Allah what is not for anyone."
